{"id":"g.math.two-var-data.3.463dd9693f","section":"math","domain":"data","skill":"two-var-data","difficulty":3,"tmpl":"math_data.residual","prompt":"The line of best fit for a data set is $y = 2x + 97$. One data point in the set is $(10, 122)$. Which statement about this data point is true?","choices":["Its $y$-value is 5 greater than the value predicted by the line of best fit.","Its $y$-value is 5 less than the value predicted by the line of best fit.","The data point lies exactly on the line of best fit.","Its $y$-value is 122 greater than the value predicted by the line of best fit."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The predicted value at $x = 10$ is $2(10) + 97 = 117$. The actual value is $122$, which is $5$ greater than the prediction."},
{"id":"g.math.two-var-data.3.59af121de4","section":"math","domain":"data","skill":"two-var-data","difficulty":3,"tmpl":"math_data.residual","prompt":"The line of best fit for a data set is $y = -1.5x + 85$. One data point in the set is $(10, 63)$. Which statement about this data point is true?","choices":["The data point lies exactly on the line of best fit.","Its $y$-value is 7 less than the value predicted by the line of best fit.","Its $y$-value is 63 less than the value predicted by the line of best fit.","Its $y$-value is 7 greater than the value predicted by the line of best fit."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The predicted value at $x = 10$ is $-1.5(10) + 85 = 70$. The actual value is $63$, which is $7$ less than the prediction."},
{"id":"g.math.two-var-data.3.3e3bf5767e","section":"math","domain":"data","skill":"two-var-data","difficulty":3,"tmpl":"math_data.residual","prompt":"The line of best fit for a data set is $y = -0.8x + 93$. One data point in the set is $(15, 85)$. Which statement about this data point is true?","choices":["Its $y$-value is 85 greater than the value predicted by the line of best fit.","Its $y$-value is 4 greater than the value predicted by the line of best fit.","Its $y$-value is 4 less than the value predicted by the line of best fit.","The data point lies exactly on the line of best fit."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The predicted value at $x = 15$ is $-0.8(15) + 93 = 81$. The actual value is $85$, which is $4$ greater than the prediction."}
